[?2004l--- PAGE 0 --- 
 Pricing Migration Rule Document
SaaS 2026 Plan Migration — Authoritative Reference
This document defines all rules governing the migration of SaaS customer accounts from legacy plans
to new 2026 pricing packages. All audit tools must use this document as the sole source of truth for
plan mapping, price floors, exception handling, [01;31m[Kgrandfather[m[King, rule precedence, and output schemas.
1. Migration Effective Date
Parameter Value
Migration effective date 2026-04-01
2. Usage Tier Calculation
Usage tier is determined from trailing 90-day API call volume ending before the migration effective date.
[36m[K--[m[K
7. Expected Monthly Price Calculation
For each account, the expected monthly price is the greater of two amounts: the plan's published base
monthly rate (Section 5) and the account's total seat-count obligation — current seats multiplied by the
per-seat floor for the applicable plan (Section 6).
Round monetary values to 2 decimal places.
8. [01;31m[KGrandfather[m[King Rules
Some accounts have a [01;31m[Kgrandfather[m[Ked_until date and a price_floor_discount_pct in their contract terms.
[01;31m[KGrandfather[m[King applies to the per-seat price floor only, not the base monthly rate or plan mapping.
When [01;31m[Kgrandfather[m[Ked_until is on or after migration_effective_date, apply price_floor_discount_pct to the
per-seat floor before computing the seat-count obligation. Normalize contract field encodings before
use.
If [01;31m[Kgrandfather[m[Ked_until is null or before migration_effective_date, [01;31m[Kgrandfather[m[King does not apply.
--- PAGE 2 --- 
 9. Exception Approval Rules
Exception approvals are stored in exception_approvals.xlsx.
An approval is valid when approval_status is approved (after normalizing case and surrounding
whitespace), effective_date is on or before migration_effective_date, and expiry_date is on or after
migration_effective_date.
A valid plan_override replaces the mapped plan. A valid price_override replaces the computed monthly
price.
10. Rule Precedence
Determine usage tier, then plan mapping, then apply valid plan overrides, then compute price from seat
floors and [01;31m[Kgrandfather[m[King, then apply valid price overrides.
11. Violation Types
Each account is assigned exactly one violation_type:
Parameter Value
no_violation Expected plan and price match assignment.
usage_tier_miscalculated Assigned plan matches wrong usage tier.
wrong_plan Assigned plan does not match expected plan, not due to usage tier.
wrong_price_floor Plan is correct, but assigned monthly price does not match expected monthly price, and the mismatch is not better explained by an expired exception or missing [01;31m[Kgrandfather[m[King.
missing_[01;31m[Kgrandfather[m[King Plan is correct, but assigned price does not reflect the [01;31m[Kgrandfather[m[King-adjusted seat floor used to compute the expected monthly price.
expired_exception Assignment relied on an approval whose expiry_date is before migration_effective_date.
12. Required Output Schemas
migration_audit.csv — one row per account:
account_id | legacy_plan | usage_tier | expected_new_plan | assigned_new_plan |
expected_monthly_price | assigned_monthly_price | migration_status | violation_type
| revenue_impact_usd
migration_status allowed values: pass, fail
violation_type allowed values: no_violation, usage_tier_miscalculated, wrong_plan, wrong_price_floor,
missing_[01;31m[Kgrandfather[m[King, expired_exception
revenue_impact_usd = assigned_monthly_price - expected_monthly_price (positive = overcharged,
negative = undercharged, zero = pass)
